{"name":"Red Orange","hex":"#ff3f34","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red-orange","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an orange hue with a hint of red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red-orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blood orange","blocks":[{"text":"The blood orange is a variety of orange with crimson flesh colored near or the same as blood. It is one of the sweet orange varieties. It is also known as the raspberry orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/BloodOrange.jpg/330px-BloodOrange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_orange","wikidata":"Q303669"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/500px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/1280px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/500px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Immature 'Moro' blood orange fruit – 7 months from flowering","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImmature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/500px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/1280px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/500px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of Sanguinello juice","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABloodorange1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Blood_orange_on_white.jpg/120px-Blood_orange_on_white.jpg?utm_sou